hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1140","Chapter mentioning Khaybar, 1180 - Abd Allah ibn Hashim narrated to us, he said: Yahya narrated to us, from Ubayd Allah, from Nafi', from Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) contracted with Khaybar for half of what comes out of it of dates or crops."
"1141","1181 - al-Rabi' informed us that Ibn Wahb narrated to them, he said: Usamah informed me, from Nafi', from Abd Allah ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: When Khaybar was conquered, the Jews asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to leave them in it on condition they work for half of what comes out of it of dates and crops. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We shall leave you in it upon that as long as we wish. They remained in it thus during the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). The dates were divided according to shares from half of Khaybar, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would take the fifth."
